# Trivy misconfiguration ignores for the repo-root scan.
#
# WHY THIS FILE EXISTS, and why the inline `#trivy:ignore:` comments in
# modules/logs-archive/main.tf are not sufficient on their own:
#
#   The CI trivy job scans from the repo root with the version trivy-action pins
#   (0.70 at the time of writing). That version does NOT honor the inline
#   `#trivy:ignore:avd-azu-0012` comment, even placed immediately above the
#   flagged resource. Verified by reproducing CI's exact invocation locally
#   against trivy 0.70.0, including a negative control: removing this file
#   restores the failure, adding it back clears it. A path-scoped
#   `.trivyignore.yaml` was tried first and is also not honored by 0.70.
#
#   The pre-commit terraform_trivy hook scans per-directory with whatever trivy
#   is installed locally, where the inline comments DO work. So both mechanisms
#   are needed: inline comments for the per-directory hook, this file for the
#   root-level CI scan.
#
# LIMITATION: entries here are repo-wide, because 0.70 ignores the path-scoped
# format. If a second storage account is ever added to this repo, AVD-AZU-0012
# will be suppressed for it too without anyone being told. Re-check this file
# when trivy-action is bumped; once the pinned version honors inline comments or
# .trivyignore.yaml, delete this file and rely on the inline ignores.
#
# BOTH id forms are listed deliberately. Trivy reports these checks as `AZU-00NN`
# in output while the canonical AVD id is `AVD-AZU-00NN`, and both forms were
# verified to work.
#
# WHY MEDIUM AND LOW CHECKS ARE LISTED HERE, even though both trivy jobs declare
# `severity: CRITICAL,HIGH`:
#
#   trivy-action's entrypoint contains this, and it is not obvious from the
#   workflow:
#
#       if [ "${TRIVY_FORMAT:-}" = "sarif" ]; then
#         if [ "${INPUT_LIMIT_SEVERITIES_FOR_SARIF:-false,,}" != "true" ]; then
#           unset TRIVY_SEVERITY
#
#   So the SARIF-format scan in push.yaml DISCARDS the declared severity filter
#   and scans ALL severities, then still honors `exit-code: 1`. That job therefore
#   effectively gates on MEDIUM and LOW too, while the table-format jobs gate only
#   on CRITICAL and HIGH. The action prints "Building SARIF report with all
#   severities" when it does this.
#
#   Consequence for anyone adding a resource here: a MEDIUM finding will turn
#   master red even though no workflow appears to ask for MEDIUM. Either accept it
#   in this file with a justification, or fix it. Setting
#   `limit-severities-for-sarif: true` on that step would restore the declared
#   policy, at the cost of the Security tab no longer receiving MEDIUM/LOW.

# Storage account network default action is Allow.
# The Datadog log-archive account must accept writes from Datadog's archive
# writer, which reaches it over the public internet and is not an Azure trusted
# service, so a Deny default action would stop archiving. Restricting it means
# allowlisting Datadog's published egress ranges, a caller-side decision that has
# to be verified against those ranges and kept current, and that fails silently
# when wrong. Access remains gated on Entra auth with only the Datadog principal
# granted blob write; account keys are disabled by default and public blob access
# is off. See modules/logs-archive/README.md.
AVD-AZU-0012
AZU-0012

# Storage account has no Storage Analytics logging enabled.
# Request-level diagnostics belong on Azure Monitor diagnostic settings, which
# this repo provisions as a first-class concern, not on legacy Storage Analytics.
AVD-AZU-0057
AZU-0057

# Storage account is not geo-redundant.
# LRS is a deliberate cost default for a multi-year archive;
# `storage_account_replication_type` exposes GRS/GZRS for callers who want
# geo-redundancy and will pay for it.
AVD-AZU-0058
AZU-0058

# Storage account does not use customer-managed keys.
# Platform-managed keys. CMK needs a Key Vault, a key, and an identity with
# wrap/unwrap, which is a caller-level decision rather than something a log-archive
# module should provision. Infrastructure encryption IS enabled, so data is
# double-encrypted at rest with platform keys.
AVD-AZU-0060
AZU-0060
